ummary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.6 beta 3\n\n### Issue description\n\nModern theme, light preset:\n\nThe contrast slider makes some elements higher contrast, and other elements lower contrast.\n\nThis means, for light mode users: There is no straightforward way to increase/decrease contrast.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n#### Default contrast for reference:\n\n<img width=\"937\" height=\"416\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/023bd9c8-aea6-4f0f-83cd-fe100a95ad41\" />\n\n#### Lower the contrast value\n\n<img width=\"937\" height=\"416\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a8dd689e-5d3d-4919-a7c0-bcf2b37eaae3\" />\n\nThe editor got brighter, which provides higher contrast.\nButtons and highlights got darker, providing higher contrast to their surroundings, but their text remained the same colour, providing _lower contrast_ to the contained text.\n\n<img width=\"922\" height=\"453\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e8a51d56-a0a5-43ee-a02a-f4b979f517ce\" />\n\nTo the extreme, this becomes unreadable.\n\n#### Increase the contrast value\n\n<img width=\"922\" height=\"453\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/441938c0-f26a-4174-8365-859db26d09e0\" />\n\nThe editor provides _lower contrast_.\nThe buttons have _higher contrast_.\n\n### Expected Behaviour\n\nTurning the slider one way should increase/decrease the contrast for everything. \nEach end of the slider should be the minimum/maximum contrast for everything.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{